'''''Hellhound Two''''', alternatively spelled '''''Hellhound 2''''', was an [[All Terrain Armored Transport]] used by the [[Galactic Empire]] during the [[Battle of Jakku]], the final [[Battle of Jakku|battle]] of the [[Galactic Civil War]]. Almost three [[Standard decade|decades]] after the battle, the AT-AT served as the home of a young [[scavenger]] named [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], who salvaged what supplies she could and lived inside of the [[walker]], which lay on its side in the [[Goazon Badlands]].

==Description==
''Hellhound Two'' was one of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s quadruped [[All Terrain Armored Transport]] combat [[walker]]s. Like other AT-ATs, the vehicle had a [[Color|grey]] hull and featured two chin-mounted heavy [[laser cannon]]s and two temple-mounted medium [[blaster]]s. The craft was operated by two [[AT-AT pilot|pilots]] and a [[Vehicle commander|commander]], and it could ferry multiple [[stormtrooper]]s.<ref name="CL" />

==History==
===Battle of Jakku===
While in Imperial service, the AT-AT was designated "Hellhound Two", and formed part of the [[Hellhound attack force]] of the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]], ''[[Interrogator]]''. The walker was deployed to the [[desert]] [[planet]] of [[Jakku]] one [[Standard year|year]] after the [[Battle of Endor]], where it went into combat against the fledgling [[New Republic]] during the [[Battle of Jakku]], the final battle of the [[Galactic Civil War]]. Its objective was to protect the [[Imperial research base]].<ref name="On the Front Lines" />

The walker was destroyed by New Republic [[RZ-1 A-wing interceptor|A-wing]] [[pilot]] [[Odavia Anaru]]. Knocked out of the sky by a surface-to-air missile in the [[Goazon Badlands]],<ref name="CL" /> Anaru was well behind enemy lines. Retreating to better cover, Anaru took a rocket launcher from a fallen trooper. Bracing the heavy weapon against a broken hull fragment, she took aim at the lead AT-AT assaulting New Republic commandos, and fired. Stormtroopers rushed her position, but Anaru didn't move, instead firing all six rockets at the AT-AT's weak points. While the walker crumbled, Odavia Anaru died in the effort, and was posthumously awarded the [[Medal of Valor]].<ref name="On the Front Lines" />

===Home of Rey===
{{Quote|I don't even think of it as sideways anymore – I've lived here long enough that it feels right that way.|Rey|<ref name="Survival Guide" />}}
[[File:Hellhound_Two_interior.png|thumb|left|300px|The interior of Rey's home.]]
Twenty-nine years after the Empire's defeat on Jakku, the young [[scavenger]] named [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] had made a home for herself in the abandoned walker. Having stripped it of its valuable parts, Rey lived in the troop compartment of AT-AT, which simultaneously served as her kitchen, workroom, and bedroom, with the latter containing a hammock. To defend against intruders, Rey had welded the walker's hatches shut, using its auxiliary hatch as an entrance. Salvaged [[fuel cell]]s from the walker's [[laser-cannon energizer]] wired up to a [[TIE series|TIE fighter's]] [[Solar collector|solar panel]] help power Rey's homemade generator. However, this required constant maintenance. She also removed the terrain sensors from the walker's feet and used them as an early motion warning system. The head with a cryptographic lock houses most of Rey's most valued items.<ref name="CL" /> When she became a [[Escape from Jakku|target]] of the [[First Order]] for being seen with [[Finn]] at [[Niima Outpost]], however, Rey had no other option than leave the AT-AT and Jakku behind to join the [[Resistance]].<ref name="TFA" /> With her long-time home now abandoned, the ''Hellhound Two'' was eventually claimed by competing scavengers of the desert world.<ref name="Rise of Skywalker Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Hellhound Two first appeared in the [[2015]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. It was originally painted in gray paint, but in the salt plains of [[Wikipedia:Abu Dhabi|Abu Dhabi]] where Jakku scenes were filmed, the set designers had to switch to a metallic paint so it was visible. A scale model of the homestead was also created.<ref name="The Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''</ref>

